"""Curated source data for the USP34 vs VEZF1 translational deep-dive phase.

Data provenance: this phase was originally scoped for four parallel
research passes (one per: USP34 tissue/muscle/genetics, VEZF1
tissue/muscle/genetics, USP34 direct/indirect targeting, VEZF1
direct/indirect targeting). All four parallel background research agents
failed mid-run because the session hit its weekly usage limit before
producing results (no data from those runs is used anywhere in this
module). Rather than fabricate the missing coverage, this module instead
combines (a) facts already gathered and verified in the prior
druggability_safety phase (src/druggability_safety_data.py -- UniProt,
PDB, AlphaFold, ChEMBL, Pharos, Open Targets, GTEx, HPA, gnomAD, OMIM,
ClinGen, MGI, IMPC, PubMed, all independently source-fetched, cited again
here rather than re-derived) with (b) a smaller, still fully
source-verified, direct research pass performed in this same session
(STRING interactome queries, targeted PubMed/eutils searches, ClinVar
counts, and re-verification fetches), prioritized toward the phase's two
highest-value NEW questions: systematic indirect-target discovery (STRING
interactors + targeted literature) and a muscle-specific literature
search for both genes. Coverage is real but narrower than the full
18-section brief requested -- this is disclosed explicitly in the report
rather than papered over with invented tissue-atlas or indirect-target
detail. Every fact below carries its exact source; anything not found is
recorded as "no relevant evidence identified in the searches performed."

GAP-COMPLETION PASS (second research session): the user asked for a
focused gap-completion and validation pass on top of the above, targeting
five specific gaps: (1) cell-type-resolved tissue atlas coverage beyond
HPA's bulk/immune panel, (2) a more systematic USP34 muscle search
including the KIAA0570/KIAA0729 aliases, (3) precise characterization of
the VEZF1/PMID 31911272 cardiac finding, (4) critical validation of the
TEAD1-VEZF1 indirect-targeting hypothesis (is there perturbation evidence,
or only a cardiac binding-partner report?), and (5) exact TEAD1
pharmacology (TEAD1-specific vs pan-TEAD, and true clinical-stage
status). All new facts from this second pass are marked "NEW (gap-pass)"
in the fields below; every claim was again independently source-verified
by direct fetch (HPA JSON API, NCBI eutils, STRING API, WebSearch of
primary sources), never recalled from memory. One claim surfaced by an
AI-summarized web search (a purported Usp34/C2C12-myoblast differential
-expression finding) could NOT be independently re-confirmed by a direct
follow-up search and is explicitly excluded from the report as
unverified, per this project's standing rule against laundering
unverified AI-search-summary claims into cited findings.
"""

